# OwlBack Cursor Rules (STRICT)

## Global Behavior
- Do NOT generate markdown files (.md)
- Do NOT generate README or documentation unless explicitly requested
- Do NOT summarize, explain, or restate requirements
- Output must be minimal and task-focused
- Prefer code or concrete conclusions only

## Output Control
- Use diff-style output whenever modifying existing code
- Do NOT repeat unchanged code
- Limit responses to what is explicitly asked
- No architectural essays or background explanations

## Project Structure
- owlRD is the single source of truth for database design and requirements
- Database schemas MUST match ../owlRD/db/*.sql exactly
- Business and technical rules MUST reference ../owlRD/docs/
- Do NOT invent tables, fields, or constraints

## Code Style
- Go version: 1.21+
- Follow standard Go project layout
- Logging: zap only
- Shared utilities: owl-common only
- No alternative libraries unless explicitly approved

## Database Rules
- PostgreSQL 15+ with TimescaleDB
- snake_case for all database fields
- UUID for all primary keys
- Schema definitions must align with ../owlRD/db/*.sql

## References (READ-ONLY)
- ../owlRD/db/*.sql
- ../owlRD/docs/06_FHIR_Simple_Conversion_Guide.md
- ../owlRD/docs/20_Card_Creation_Rules_Final.md
- ../owlRD/docs/25_Alarm_Notification_Flow.md

## Prohibited Behavior
- No auto-generated documentation
- No speculative features
- No file-wide rewrites unless explicitly requested
